n.","Provisional: conditioning a convolution update on its incoming state may improve ranking. No supplied measurement establishes that this capability is missing.","The supplied graph shows no SUPERSEDES or ALTERNATIVE_TO edge or retired revision; unavailable readout hashes are not treated as evidence."],"protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","status":"unknown","suspected_capability":"Conditioning each causal convolution residual update on the state entering its block.","task_context":"The current model adds each causal convolution update to its block input. The proposed gate tests whether input-dependent scaling of that update helps next-item ranking. Prior graph comparisons test local change and direct item identity, not this block-level interaction; their failed selection does not refute this hypothesis."},"generated_controls":[{"file":"control-1.py","model_version":"amazon-next-v9-round-13-control-1"}],"host_bound_output":true,"insertion_contract_format":{"allowed_methods":["NextItNetBlock.__init__","NextItNetBlock._causal_conv","NextItNetBlock.forward","NextItNetModel.__init__","NextItNetModel.encode_sequence","NextItNetModel.forward","NextItNetModel.score_candidates"],"instructions":"Proposal.insertion_contract MUST be a JSON-encoded object with exactly schema, allowed_methods (nonempty subset of this catalog), rationale. Declare all methods the candidate AND generated controls may change, including initialization. Experiment edits outside these methods or comment-only changes are rejected before CPU admission. Other proposal fields explain the mechanism and falsification; method scope is not causal proof.","schema":"nextitnet-method-scope-v1"},"instructions":["Implement the frozen proposal and each named control; do not redesign the hypothesis or run training.","Preserve imports, module settings, training helpers and score/encode consistency. changed_files must exactly match model.py followed by generated control files.","Source changes must stay inside insertion_contract_format; report actual checks and remaining limitations."],"method":{"cost":"One learned hidden-width vector and elementwise operations per block in each new arm. GPU runtime is unmeasured. Reserve 1000000 budget units for four development fits per arm, conditional confirmation fits, missing incumbent confirmation fits, and overhead; host costing must verify sufficiency.","insertion_points":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__ and NextItNetBlock.forward","control-1.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__ and NextItNetBlock.forward"],"mechanism":"Agent hypothesis. Let x be the block input and y its existing causal convolution update. Add 0.1 × tanh(g ⊙ tanh(x)) ⊙ y to the incumbent output x + y, with learned channel vector g initialized to zero. The matched control substitutes tanh(y) for tanh(x), retaining the same vector, initialization, scale, and operations. This contrasts conditioning on the incoming state with conditioning on the update itself.","method_id":"input_conditioned_conv_residual_v1","origin":"agent_hypothesis","prerequisites":["Host source admission and CPU contracts pass.","Each category and seed starts from an independent initialization.","Host costing confirms that complete frozen-protocol fits and conditional confirmation fit within the budget."],"sources":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__ and NextItNetBlock.forward, inspected incumbent source.","context.json#/evidence_graph/nodes/current-baseline-630a86e961d313cdee43ce8e, audited local development baseline.","context.json#/evidence_graph/nodes/amazon-research-93e61b5cbad938a4-9123afb02df26f76-development and amazon-research-a907a013823c2c31-8f30ce414f70fcc2-development, prior local comparisons.","No external paper claim is made."],"tensor_constraints":["Preserve [batch, length, hidden] causal representations and zero output at padding positions.","Initialize g to zero so both new arms equal the incumbent before learning.","Use the same channel count